# SourceTrack — AI / crawler visibility (bot fetches of customer pages).
#
# DELIBERATELY SEPARATE FROM `events`. A crawler fetch is not a visit: writing
# these rows into `events` would put them inside every visitor, session, top-page
# and attribution aggregate that reads that table. Keeping bots OUT of `events`
# is the entire reason api/lib/bot-filter.js drops JS-rendering search bots at
# ingestion (incident 2026-07-14); this datasource must not reintroduce the
# pollution through the back door. Nothing here joins to `events`.
#
# Not a revenue rail: no conversion_value, no currency, no attribution columns.
# A crawler hit can never become revenue and must never be summed as such (§6).
#
# PRIVACY (§6, §6.5): no raw IP column, by design. The request IP is an INPUT to
# verification (api/lib/ai-crawler-detect.js) and is discarded at ingest — only
# the resulting verdict is stored. No visitor_id / distinct_id / anonymous_id:
# a bot is not a person, so nothing here is subject-linkable, which is also why
# this table is intentionally OUTSIDE the three GDPR paths (no PII column exists
# to erase). site_id keeps it tenant-scoped; site_key is never stored (§6.5).
#
# MergeTree, append-only, same as `events`.

TOKEN "dual_write_append" APPEND

SCHEMA >
    `site_id` String `json:$.site_id`,
    `timestamp` DateTime64(3, 'UTC') `json:$.timestamp` CODEC(DoubleDelta, ZSTD(1)),

    # Identity of the crawler, straight from the ai-crawler-detect registry.
    `bot_name` LowCardinality(String) `json:$.bot_name`,
    `operator` LowCardinality(String) `json:$.operator`,
    # llm_crawler | ai_search | ai_assistant | search_engine | seo_tool
    `category` LowCardinality(String) `json:$.category`,

    # HOW MUCH THE ROW CAN BE TRUSTED — a first-class stored column, not a
    # runtime inference. Values (api/lib/ai-crawler-detect.js VERIFICATION):
    #   ip_verified                  — UA matched AND source IP fell inside the
    #                                  operator's published range.
    #   ip_mismatch                  — UA claimed this bot from OUTSIDE the
    #                                  published range. An impersonation signal;
    #                                  must never be counted as the real bot.
    #   ua_only                      — operator publishes ranges but no check was
    #                                  possible for this request.
    #   ua_only_no_ranges_published  — operator publishes nothing; UA match is the
    #                                  strongest signal that will ever exist.
    # Stored per row so a reader can never present a UA-only count as verified.
    `verification` LowCardinality(String) `json:$.verification`,

    # Which page the crawler fetched, and what the origin answered. Path only —
    # query strings are stripped at ingest so no UTM/PII rides along.
    `path` String `json:$.path`,
    `status_code` UInt16 `json:$.status_code`,

    # Where the observation came from, so coverage gaps are legible in the data
    # rather than assumed: edge_middleware | cdn_log | origin_log | server_api.
    `collection_source` LowCardinality(String) `json:$.collection_source`

ENGINE "MergeTree"
ENGINE_PARTITION_KEY "toYYYYMM(timestamp)"
ENGINE_SORTING_KEY "site_id, timestamp, bot_name"
